          <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;">
            All weak acid is converted to its conjugate base (A⁻). This base undergoes hydrolysis in water: A⁻ + H₂O &hArr; HA + OH⁻, creating hydroxide ions and raising the pH above 7.
          </p>
